Example <p>The following code shows how <code>with_object_t</code> can be used to create a JSON type that stores object elements in a <code>std::map</code> and therefore keeps them sorted by key, unlike the default type which preserves insertion order only when <code>nlohmann::ordered_json</code> is used.</p> <pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;
