Example: default behavior <p>The following code will trigger an assertion at runtime:</p> <pre><code>#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;

using nlohmann::json;

int main()
{
    const json j = {{"key", "value"}};
    auto v = j["missing"];
}
</code></pre> <p>Output:</p> <pre><code>Assertion failed: (m_value.object-&gt;find(key) != m_value.object-&gt;end()), function operator[], file json.hpp, line 2144.
</code></pre> Example: user-defined behavior <p>The assertion reporting can be changed by defining <code>JSON_ASSERT(x)</code> differently.</p> <pre><code>#include &lt;cstdio&gt;
#include &lt;cstdlib&gt;
#define JSON_ASSERT(x) if(!(x)){fprintf(stderr, "assertion error in %s\n", __FUNCTION__); std::abort();}

#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;

using nlohmann::json;

int main()
{
    const json j = {{"key", "value"}};
    auto v = j["missing"];
}
</code></pre> <p>Output:</p> <pre><code>assertion error in operator[]
</code></pre>

Example: default behavior (macro not defined) <p>Without the macro, single-element brace initialization wraps the value in an array:</p> <pre><code>#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;

using nlohmann::json;

int main()
{
    json obj = {{"key", "value"}};

    json j{obj};
    // j is [{"key":"value"}]  -- single-element array, NOT a copy of obj
}
</code></pre> Example: opt-in copy semantics (macro defined to 1) <p>With the macro, single-element brace initialization copies/moves the value:</p> <pre><code>#define JSON_BRACE_INIT_COPY_SEMANTICS 1
#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;

using nlohmann::json;

int main()
{
    json obj = {{"key", "value"}};

    json j{obj};
    // j is {"key":"value"}  -- copy of obj
}
</code></pre>

Example: default behavior (macro not defined) <p>Without the macro, the deprecated overload is called, and the compiler warns about it:</p> <pre><code>#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;

using nlohmann::json;

int main()
{
    const std::vector&lt;std::uint8_t&gt; v = {0x82, 0x01, 0x02};
    auto j = json::from_cbor(v.data(), v.size());
    // warning: 'from_cbor' is deprecated: Since 3.8.0; use from_cbor(ptr, ptr + len)
}
</code></pre> Example: deleted deprecated functions (macro defined to 1) <p>With the macro, the call does not compile:</p> <pre><code>#define JSON_DELETE_DEPRECATED_FUNCTIONS 1
#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;

using nlohmann::json;

int main()
{
    const std::vector&lt;std::uint8_t&gt; v = {0x82, 0x01, 0x02};
    auto j = json::from_cbor(v.data(), v.size());
    // error: call to deleted function 'from_cbor'
}
</code></pre>

